        },
        {
          "name": "GaN",
          "role": "uncertain"
        },
        {
          "name": "AlN",
          "role": "uncertain"
        }
      ],
      "numeric_roles": {
        "cited_result": 2,
        "uncertain": 7,
        "experimental_condition": 6,
        "simulation_parameter": 1
      },
      "numeric_candidates": [
        {
          "candidate_index": 0,
          "role": "cited_result",
          "reason": "explicit_prior_work_context",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e32"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [
            "e102"
          ],
          "text": "It is\nperhaps best known for giving rise to the 694.3 nm (1.786 eV) emission in Cr-doped Al2O3, exploited in ruby\nlasers.",
          "pages": [
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 1,
          "role": "cited_result",
          "reason": "explicit_prior_work_context",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e33"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [
            "e103"
          ],
          "text": "Cr possesses a quartet ground-state spin and has an internal transition with a zero-phonon\nline near 1.8 eV.",
          "pages": [
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 2,
          "role": "uncertain",
          "reason": "insufficient_or_mixed_numeric_context",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e34"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [],
          "text": "Monoclinic Ga2O3 (β-Ga2O3) has garnered attention\nfor its ability to be controllably n-type-doped despite\nits ultra-wide (∼4.9 eV) bandgap.1,2 Its high breakdown\nfield and availability of high-quality low-cost substrates\nmake it an excellent material for high-power electron-\nics and ultraviolet optoelectronics.1,3–5 These properties\nalso render β-Ga2O3 a suitable host for quantum de-\nfects.6,7 Realizing any of these applications in β-Ga2O3\ndemands control over the native point defects and impu-\nrities present in the crystal and a deeper understanding\nof their electrical and optical properties relevant for spin\nand photonic qubits.8",
          "pages": [
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 3,
          "role": "uncertain",
          "reason": "insufficient_or_mixed_numeric_context",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e35"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [],
          "text": "We study the excited-\nstate structure and find an internal transition between\na 2E excited state and 4A2 ground state near 1.8 eV.",
          "pages": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 4,
          "role": "uncertain",
          "reason": "insufficient_or_mixed_numeric_context",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e36"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [],
          "text": "The agreement provides compelling evidence that the ob-\nserved spectrum, with a zero-phonon line (ZPL) at 1.79\neV, is indeed due to substitutional Cr on an octahedral\nsite.",
          "pages": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 5,
          "role": "experimental_condition",
          "reason": "experimental_procedure",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e38"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [],
          "text": "A single crystal sample of β-Ga2O3 was grown via the\nfloating zone method, using a locally designed laser float-\ning zone furnace “LOKII” in the Wilson lab at UC Santa\nBarbara.23 In preparation for the crystal growth, poly-\ncrystalline powder of Ga2O3 (99.99 %, Alfa Aesar) was\ndried overnight at 1200 ◦C and then packed in a rubber\nballoon with a diameter of 4 mm.",
          "pages": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 6,
          "role": "experimental_condition",
          "reason": "experimental_procedure",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e39"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [],
          "text": "The packed powder in\nthe balloon was pressed into a 90 mm long rod using a\ncold isostatic press.",
          "pages": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 7,
          "role": "experimental_condition",
          "reason": "experimental_procedure",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e40"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [],
          "text": "The rod was then broken into two\npieces, measuring 65 mm and 25 mm in length.",
          "pages": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 8,
          "role": "experimental_condition",
          "reason": "experimental_procedure",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e41"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [],
          "text": "Growth conditions were\nkept constant throughout the process, including a trans-\nlation rate of 15 mm/hr for both the seed and feed rods, a\nrotation rate of 10 rpm, and a total incident laser power\nof 168 W.",
          "pages": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 9,
          "role": "uncertain",
          "reason": "insufficient_or_mixed_numeric_context",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e42"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [],
          "text": "The length of the single crystal of β-Ga2O3\nis 60 mm as shown in Fig. 1.",
          "pages": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 10,
          "role": "uncertain",
          "reason": "insufficient_or_mixed_numeric_context",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e44"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [],
          "text": "phases making up less than 1% of the crystal.",
          "pages": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 11,
          "role": "experimental_condition",
          "reason": "experimental_procedure",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e45"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [],
          "text": "To characterize the optical properties of the grown β-\nGa2O3 sample at wavelengths in the visible spectrum,\nphotoluminescence spectroscopy was performed at 4.2 K\nusing a 532 nm laser diode as an excitation source.",
          "pages": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 12,
          "role": "experimental_condition",
          "reason": "experimental_procedure",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e46"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [],
          "text": "A low-pass fil-\nter at 550 nm is used to block the residual laser light.",
          "pages": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 13,
          "role": "uncertain",
          "reason": "insufficient_or_mixed_numeric_context",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e47"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [],
          "text": "A sharp line at 1.79 eV associated\nwith the zero-phonon line is found, as well as several\nsmaller peaks at lower energy.",
          "pages": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 14,
          "role": "uncertain",
          "reason": "mixed_result_condition_or_comparison",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e48"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [],
          "text": "The screening parameter is\nset to the default value, and we tune the mixing pa-\nrameter to 32%, resulting in a bandgap of 4.83 eV in\ngood agreement with the experimental value of 4.9 eV.2",
          "pages": [
            3
          ]
        },
        {
          "candidate_index": 15,
          "role": "simulation_parameter",
          "reason": "computational_procedure",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "e49"
          ],
          "context_evidence_ids": [],
          "text": "The wavefunctions were expanded in a plane-wave basis\nwith an energy cutoff of 400 eV.",
          "pages": [
            3
          ]
        }
      ],
      "exact_slices_verified": 103,
      "missing_core_fields": []
